1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,620
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,537
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,955
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,400
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,000
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:24,197
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:26,357
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,560
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:35,180
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,420
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,660
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:52,537
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:58,437
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:03,877
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:10,137
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,417
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

20
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,777
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:21,257
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:24,220
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:28,197
So come aboard and bring along.

24
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,540
All your hopes and dreams.

25
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,817
Together we will find everything.

26
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,980
That we're looking for.

27
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,617
There's always room for you.

28
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,400
If you wanna be my friend.

29
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:46,860
We are, we are on the cruise.

30
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,680
We are.

31
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,800
What was that?

32
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,260
It's Sorcery!

33
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:00,657
Oh, he's a freak!

34
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:02,020
A magical freak!

35
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:04,040
He sent Captain Kaido fine!

36
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,427
I'll just leave this to you.

37
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,869
I've got treasure to find.

38
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,120
Use our pirates!

39
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:33,220
Have a ride!

40
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:37,360
No, don't! Stay away!

41
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:40,280
Say your prayers, butler! Take that!

42
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,440
And that!

43
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:45,480
Game over, you lousy,
Newgate pirate! No! Stop it!

44
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,780
Those kids! What are they doing?

45
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:53,177
Those Rugrats have a death wish.

46
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,757
You don't know what you're doing!

47
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:55,670
Stop!

48
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:56,850
Stop!

49
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:00,790
All right.

50
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:03,757
This time we'll let you off
without any more brutality.

51
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,680
This time.

52
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,097
Now those stupid kids have really done it.

53
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:10,239
Captain Kuro is going to be so mad.

54
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,537
Captain! I knew it!

55
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:14,450
You were fighting!

56
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:15,657
Gosh, that is so totally awesome!

57
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:17,957
I thought there were no
secrets between us pirates.

58
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,097
Why didn't you tell us?

59
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,010
That's right!

60
00:03:20,093 --> 00:03:22,997
We're supposed to tell each other
everything cares about that.

61
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:24,492
Look, this is important.

62
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,699
You guys got to get out of here run

63
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,617
We have to stand fight
with you do you thought

64
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:34,053
pirates will be shamed if we run in fear

65
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,270
Captain!

66
00:04:01,353 --> 00:04:02,183
Captain!

67
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,120
That hurt.

68
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:08,730
Hmm.

69
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,050
My, my.

70
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:13,117
That's quite a strange technique
you've developed there.

71
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,259
Tell me something.

72
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:17,157
Do you have powers from
eating the Devil Fruit?

73
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,070
Yep.

74
00:04:18,153 --> 00:04:19,820
I'm a rubber man.

75
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,657
He ate the Devil Fruit.

76
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:26,597
That guy's dangerous.

77
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,737
Those Devil Fruit people are real.

78
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:29,197
He's got rubber arms of death.

79
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,617
It makes perfect sense now.

80
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:34,171
I didn't just hallucinate his
arm stretching out like that.

81
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,590
Jungle.

82
00:04:36,673 --> 00:04:37,503
Sir.

83
00:04:37,586 --> 00:04:38,980
I can handle the boy.

84
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,600
You take care of Miss
Kaya like we planned.

85
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:45,934
Have her ride her butler into her will?

86
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,140
Then kill her.

87
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,980
As for the kids, they're an eyesore.

88
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,522
Eliminate them.

89
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:57,660
I'm on it.

90
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:03,860
Stop right there.

91
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,417
If you want to get to them, you'll
have to make it through me first.

92
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,330
Huh?

93
00:05:08,413 --> 00:05:09,243
Geek!

94
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,060
Star-sipper!

95
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:17,010
Not again.

96
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:56,217
that guy he's crazy oh no kaya

97
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:59,177
no stay away from

98
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:03,800
her no don't no

99
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:10,380
OOSA PIRATES!

100
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,180
Yes, sir!

101
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:16,580
I need you to listen carefully.

102
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,400
Look, we're not running.

103
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,337
Not after they did this to you.

104
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,600
We will avenge you.

105
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,140
Protect Kaya.

106
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,200
Do as I say.

107
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,180
Don't argue with me.

108
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:33,932
I'm giving you the most important
task there is right now.

109
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:37,120
It's absolutely critical that you succeed.

110
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,940
Take Kaya and get away from here.

111
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,800
You must keep her safe.

112
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,849
This is the reason we
wanted to be pirates.

113
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:46,726
To protect what's dear to us.

114
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,420
So do as I say.

115
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,680
And run!

116
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:53,530
Usa.

117
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,580
Now go.

118
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:04,240
That's a direct order. Yes! Captain!

119
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:08,740
Kaya, hurry! This way! Come on! Let's go!

120
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,547
He sure got away with words.

121
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:12,820
He made running away sound brave.

122
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,157
I know these words like
the back of my hand.

123
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,070
Okay.

124
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:20,370
Jungle.

125
00:07:20,453 --> 00:07:21,968
Yeah, sorry, I was gawking.

126
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:26,012
Those fools, do they really
think that they can escape me?

127
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:32,050
Gotcha.

128
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,260
Damn you!

129
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,200
He's not a priority right now.

130
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,510
Yes, sir!

131
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,980
Their attempt at escape is futile.

132
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:48,300
We know all too well how weak Kaeya is.

133
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:51,680
There is no way they can
possibly escape Jango.

134
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,054
Now, if you want to help her, go ahead.

135
00:07:56,560 --> 00:08:00,220
But first, you'll have to get
off this hill alive, Usopp.

136
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,080
Huh, Bucci!

137
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,718
I guess losing to me once
wasn't enough for you, huh?

138
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:16,311
I told you to get out of my
way, you fooling tub of a lord!

139
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,180
Now I'm blown!

140
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:31,050
Aaaah!

141
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:05,517
Honey, is that weird
hypnotist guy still behind us?

142
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:06,430
I don't know.

143
00:09:06,513 --> 00:09:07,457
I can't see him anymore.

144
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,057
Let's make sure and lose it for good.

145
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:12,657
There's no way that nutjob could
catch up to us in our own forest.

146
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:14,217
Don't you worry, Miss Kaya.

147
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,817
The Oshoff pirates are going
to keep you safe and sound.

148
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:17,730
That's right.

149
00:09:17,813 --> 00:09:19,934
The Oshoff pirates stand by their word.

150
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:23,020
Thank you so much.

151
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:48,260
Well, they're not there.

152
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,040
Bulls, I'm coming to get you!

153
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:54,573
Do you really think you can run from me?

154
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,920
We could do this the easy way?

155
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,632
or I could just level this entire forest!

156
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,000
Whoa, that guy is really mad.

157
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:09,379
And he can do a lot more
than just hypnotize people.

158
00:10:14,020 --> 00:10:15,860
Where have you gone?

159
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,997
Wait, what was that sound?

160
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:31,300
That is the sound of destruction.

161
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:34,432
Jungo's probably tearing the place apart.

162
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:35,740
Go ahead.

163
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:38,740
See for yourself if you can get up.

164
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,357
Heartless bastard,

165
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:48,557
don't you even have a shred of pity you
lived with that girl for three years?

166
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:52,717
No, I've told you Kaya is nothing
more than a pawn in the game.

167
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:57,180
I intend to win when she's dead
then I'll be grateful to her.

168
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,020
Damn you.

169
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:03,280
This guy is hopelessly evil.

170
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,718
We should put him out of his misery.

171
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:07,730
Hey!

172
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:10,210
Usa!

173
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:12,180
Go find the others!

174
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,520
Don't worry.

175
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,407
We'll take care of this guy.

176
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,090
Go on.

177
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:32,317
Ah very impressive you can still move.

178
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,737
Shut up!

179
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,957
You won't get away with this!

180
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:39,277
I won't let you.

181
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:42,277
You betrayed the villagers'
trust not to mention

182
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:45,184
you plan to take the life
of a sweet young girl.

183
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,090
No!

184
00:11:47,173 --> 00:11:49,560
This is the last time
you ever get your way!

185
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:53,090
Usopp!

186
00:11:58,260 --> 00:11:59,090
It hurts.

187
00:11:59,173 --> 00:12:00,797
It hurts so bad.

188
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,160
I can't move.

189
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,260
You really are a riot.

190
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,720
Just stay on the ground there.

191
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,791
Even if you did somehow catch up to Jango,

192
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,491
he'd end your life in the blink of an eye.

193
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,076
Staying there is what's best for you.

194
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,480
I don't care.

195
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,110
Hm?

196
00:12:29,193 --> 00:12:30,880
I don't care that I'm weak.

197
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,220
I'll protect them.

198
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,860
I'm captain of the Usopp Pirates.

199
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,057
A brave warrior of the sea who
fights for what he holds dear.

200
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:42,316
I will protect everyone in
the village if it kills me.

201
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:47,320
On my word, you will never
set foot in that village!

202
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,000
What's his deal?

203
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:56,717
He's yelling about something.

204
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,329
Check it out, he's crying.

205
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:12,800
What's so funny?

206
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:19,997
Luffy, me and Usopp are going
to chase down that hypno-freak.

207
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:22,460
Is that a problem? No. Hurry!

208
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,480
Hey, thank you.

209
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:27,677
I'd be a whole lot faster
if I was going by myself.

210
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,297
But I don't know those woods.

211
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:32,497
So if we're going to catch up to
them, I'm going to need your help.

212
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,580
Hold it, you two.

213
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,597
Where do you think you're going?

214
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:38,840
Who gave you permission
to go anywhere? I did!

215
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,480
Miss, Zoro, get going!

216
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,040
Have another!

217
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,210
Gums!

218
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,300
Man, he disappeared again!

219
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,300
The others got away.

220
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,777
That's the most important thing, really.

221
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:06,900
Before I kill you, I
feel compelled to ask.

222
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:11,557
What is an outsider like you budding
into this village's business for?

223
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:16,057
Because there's a man in this
village that I don't want to let die.

224
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:21,457
Simple enough are you okay with
that being the reason that you die?

225
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:23,157
Sure am.

226
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:25,437
But I'm not gonna die.

227
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,360
We'll see about that.

228
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:47,720
This is quite boring.

229
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,040
You cocky jerk.

230
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,380
Go east.

231
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:58,937
Hey, I said go east, so go east already.

232
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,357
This is the wrong direction.

233
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,270
Fine, east.

234
00:15:01,353 --> 00:15:03,200
Is that left or right? Turn right.

235
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,165
But that's where we came from.

236
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,740
Ms. Kaya!

237
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:12,780
I'm sorry.

238
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,940
You should go on without me.

239
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,717
What are you talking about?

240
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,212
We're under strict orders to protect you.

241
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:20,890
Oh, no.

242
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,697
She's got a really bad fever.

243
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:23,610
What?

244
00:15:23,693 --> 00:15:25,160
Hang in there, Kaya. A doctor.

245
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,157
We need a doctor.

246
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,070
You idiot.

247
00:15:27,153 --> 00:15:28,337
We don't have time for that.

248
00:15:28,420 --> 00:15:30,126
Someone's trying to kill her.

249
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,871
But it's dangerous for her to run anymore.

250
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,097
Yeah, but...

251
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:36,240
Show yourselves, you ruts.

252
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:47,000
Thank you for helping me.

253
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,180
Just the thought is more than enough.

254
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,780
Now go, all of you.

255
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,580
Where did you brats go?

256
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:02,580
If we left Kaya and ran away right
now, we would probably survive, right?

257
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,360
Yeah, probably.

258
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:07,537
And our captain always
said to run with your tail

259
00:16:07,620 --> 00:16:10,497
between your legs if you
think you're gonna lose?

260
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:12,740
Then again our captain is a liar!

261
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:18,057
But even he didn't take
his own advice he tried

262
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:21,300
so hard to protect us he
risked his life for us!

263
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,277
Swore to protect Kyle.

264
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,980
All right, then prepare
yourselves to stop pirates.

265
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:30,197
We gotta fight him.

266
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,440
Let's do it Stop this!

267
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,777
You're no match for him!

268
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:34,860
You're only kids!

269
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:37,517
You mustn't put your life
on the line for my sake!

270
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:40,894
If we don't want to die, we
have to fight for our lives!

271
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:43,170
Oh...

272
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:44,960
He nicked me!

273
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:46,980
Kuro laid him out flat!

274
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,496
Lot of good that Devil Fruit did him!

275
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:51,820
Yeah, that's Captain Kuro for ya!

276
00:16:58,940 --> 00:16:59,897
Shut up!

277
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:01,940
Don't call me that!

278
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:06,000
You still don't get it.

279
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:07,860
You fools.

280
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:12,920
This whole plan was devised so that I
may be rid of that name once and for all.

281
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:16,000
I'm tired of it.

282
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,817
Concocting plans every day for a bunch of

283
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:22,724
barbarians who care only
about havoc and mayhem.

284
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:27,017
Relentlessly attacked by
government dogs and bounty hunters.

285
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:28,397
I'm tired of it.

286
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:31,600
I am sick and tired of
that entire cursed life!

287
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:37,860
The Navy, huh?

288
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:42,020
This is the third time this week.

289
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,102
Well, can you really blame them?

290
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:48,897
You're one of the most famous
pirates sailing the seas right now.

291
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:50,860
Captain Kuro is a superstar.

292
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,560
You're right.

293
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:56,160
My infamy is what draws them to us.

294
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,760
That's why I'm going to
give up being Captain Kuro.

295
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,837
Yeah, wouldn't that be nice!

296
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:10,120
Except, the marines won't stop their
pursuit until Captain Kuro is dead.

297
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:16,517
I am going to die.

298
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:21,660
It would seem that the tumultuous
life of a pirate just isn't for me.

299
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,737
You can't quit, sir!

300
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:25,349
You're the ship's captain.

301
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,800
You can be captain now.

302
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:31,740
I have finally grown weary of this life.

303
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:36,220
It's over.

304
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:39,000
I'm killing myself for all to see.

305
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:42,360
Sir! Captain Kuro! Captain! Captain!

306
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:45,140
How many vessels are there? One!

307
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:46,357
Just one this time!

308
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:47,617
What should we do, captain?

309
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:48,697
Should we man the cannons?

310
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,217
We can blast them to splinters!

311
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:54,500
Lower a small boat into the
water. What? A boat! Now!

312
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:02,560
Vice Captain Django, Captain Kuro
just... Yeah, I know. Yeah, I know.

313
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:05,057
It's too dangerous for him
to go there by himself.

314
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:07,375
Don't tell me he's turning himself in.

315
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,230
What?

316
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,900
The cannon fire stopped.

317
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,860
Prepare to board the ship.

318
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:28,597
But, shouldn't we...

319
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:29,937
I didn't ask for your opinion.

320
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:31,680
That's an order. Yes, sir.

321
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,997
Better get ready for a fight, boys.

322
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,480
So that's why you... On three!

323
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:48,760
The Marines.

324
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:51,920
They've been wiped out.

325
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,800
Now, then, let's begin this plan.

326
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:08,080
Come on, pull yourself together.

327
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,620
I was kind enough to let
you and you alone survive.

328
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:14,540
Just do it.

329
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:18,220
I'm not kneeling to you.

330
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:21,820
Finish me off and get it over with.

331
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,820
You'll be perfect.

332
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:30,794
If you can still howl this much with
a shattered jaw, you should do fine!

333
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,757
Today is the greatest day of your life.

334
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,577
Today is the day you
captured Captain Kuro.

335
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:41,600
You should be ever so grateful to me.

336
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:46,237
I'm giving you the head of Captain Kuro.

337
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:48,837
Your name is Captain Kuro.

338
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:51,277
Your name is Captain Kuro.

339
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:53,997
This atrocity was your doing.

340
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,437
One.

341
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:56,577
Two.

342
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:58,177
Django.

343
00:20:58,260 --> 00:21:00,797
My name is Captain Kuro.

344
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,757
This atrocity was my doing.

345
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:08,217
And you are the brave marine who
caught the infamous Captain Kuro.

346
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,237
Return to base and see
that he gets executed.

347
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:12,237
One.

348
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,177
Two.

349
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,637
Django.

350
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:18,877
I am the brave marine who caught
the infamous Captain Kuro?

351
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:21,420
You're doing it again, Vice Captain.

352
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,090
Perfect.

353
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:25,200
When my double gets executed,

354
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:30,247
Captain Kuro will disappear from the
Earth, and I will live the life I deserve.

355
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:34,540
And when my plan succeeds today,

356
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:37,857
after three years of planning,
revising, and waiting,

357
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:40,352
my goal will be achieved in its entirety.

358
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:43,680
Wealth and peace of mind
will finally be mine.

359
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,897
Do you understand now, boy?

360
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:50,280
I will not allow this perfect
plan years in the making to fail.

361
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:55,120
My plan will not be disrupted
by an urchin like you!

362
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:04,617
It would seem that you can do
a lot more than just stretch.

363
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:05,530
That's right.

364
00:22:05,613 --> 00:22:08,700
I've been toughening
myself up to be a pirate

365
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:14,840
Know what don't want a reputation

366
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,900
Then don't be a pirate!

367
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:26,140
You're just greedy, Kuro.

368
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:28,420
But I have ambition!

369
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:37,857
As a kid, I never stopped.

370
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,477
Searching for a great treasure.

371
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:45,257
I had a map in my mind.

372
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:47,937
That I knew would leave me.

373
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:52,037
I had to find my way to that place.

374
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:54,937
Before someone could beat me.

375
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:59,117
The promised land was in my grasp.

376
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:01,460
And I wouldn't let go.

377
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:05,577
La la la la.

378
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:06,937
My only dream.

379
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:09,180
La la la la la.

380
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:14,720
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true.

381
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:23,477
But if the world ever
changes, I call out your name.

382
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:30,397
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

383
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:37,160
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

384
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:42,480
Waiting for that one true dream?
